        "id": 229648,
        "name": "MindWanderer",
        "username": "MindWanderer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/{size}/4816_2.png",
        "created_at": "2020-01-28T20:47:23.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Not a dev, and it looks like you're using an older version of the document, but taking a look at those:</p>\n<ol>\n\t<li>A subset of heroes, or all heroes and also all villains and NPC's, seem about equally balanced to me.</li>\n\t<li>I agree, it's confusing.&nbsp; \"Threats\" can be minions, lieutenants, or villains, and bringing in a die's worth of villains doesn't make a ton of sense here.</li>\n\t<li>That's probably intentional, but same as the base scene makes sense.</li>\n\t<li>This was fixed in the most recent version.</li>\n</ol>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:04:27.342Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
